The Responses-to-Chat conversion design is informed by codex-deepseek-proxy
(MIT License, copyright 2026 Codex DeepSeek Proxy Contributors):
https://github.com/himmetozcan/codex-deepseek-proxy

The implementation in this repository was rewritten for the PCL Tailnet
gateway and adds model discovery, a management-only MCP server, client
installers, and a native Codex v1 sub-agent integration.

The unified model catalog, official Codex forward-header allowlist, native v1
sub-agent routing, health surface, and dashboard information architecture were
informed by and selectively migrated from
OpenCodex (MIT License, copyright 2026 opencodex contributors):
https://github.com/lidge-jun/opencodex

PCL Relay keeps a narrower personal-Tailnet scope: it does not import or
manage the user's OpenAI credentials. OpenCodex is not installed or required at
runtime; the integrated implementation is shipped as part of PCL Relay.

Codex transport compatibility details including zstd request bodies, websocket
prewarm fallback, and spawn-agent catalog priority were cross-checked against
CCSwitchMulti (MIT License, copyright 2025 Jason Young):
https://github.com/BigStrongSun/ccswitchmulti
